<%# The latest closed bar's O/H/L/C and volume (CKP-2), read as one inline line
    next to the range control — the shape every chart puts there. One row, not
    the range's aggregate: it answers "what did the last session do", which is
    the question that belongs beside a window control.

    D10: the card's heading already declares the currency, so the rows drop the
    prefix. Repeating `USD` four times is what that rule exists to stop.
    Locals: bar, currency. %>
<dl class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-x-3 gap-y-1 font-mono">
  <% { o: bar.open, h: bar.high, l: bar.low, c: bar.close }.each do |key, value| %>
    <div class="flex items-baseline gap-1">
      <dt class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-fg-subtle">
        <%= t("market.precio.ohlc.#{key}") %>
      </dt>
      <dd class="text-xs font-semibold text-fg-default">
        <%= value ? bare_amount_mx(value) : "—" %>
      </dd>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <div class="flex items-baseline gap-1">
    <dt class="text-[10px] uppercase tracking-[0.08em] text-fg-subtle">
      <%= t("market.precio.ohlc.vol") %>
    </dt>
    <dd class="text-xs font-semibold text-fg-default">
      <%= bar.volume ? format_compact_count(bar.volume) : "—" %>
    </dd>
  </div>
</dl>
